      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am not a avatar builder myself, I am a world creator, however I do know of a way to fix commissioners from logging into other users accounts, this is as far as I'm aware against TOS but commissioners still do so for the reason they do not want their assets shared/stolen.\n\nAnd due to this is a Commissioner logs into the users account and all users they have logged into if they ever happened to get banned all the accounts they logged into also get banned. As well as they have access to remove your account knowing your details.\n\nTo fix this I propose a Avatar SDK 3.0 Fix where a new Upload type is Set. So Public Avatars Can be cloned, Private Avatars Cannot be cloned. However Implementing a Semi-Private avatar that can be grabbed off pedestals but disallow public cloning would be a solution for all the avatar creators content being stolen from commissions, This would allow creators to Sell their avatars in private worlds they invite them to their private world into inside VRC and clone that avatar then the user would not be able to join again due to the private world restriction. I think this would also offer as a Inside Game Shop solution as well for avatar creators without a need for a actual shop Tab Window at the moment.",
